#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:12
#: 60759eb3c0f6453d8b3fbe7dc1f4e7b2
msgid ""
"Normal Flying-wing aircraft uses two control surfaces as Elevons to control "
"pitch and roll. In some cases, rudders are added to the winglets to control "
"yaw. Differential spoiler takes advantage of splitting elevons into 4 "
"independent control surfaces: normal elevon functions are reserved for pitch"
" and roll control, but yaw control is done by using two surfaces on one side"
" of the wing to create drag force thus controlling yaw motion, emulating "
"rudder control. If calibrated correctly, it will ensure pilot has smooth yaw"
" control via rudder input during take-off and landing as well as allowing "
"the pilot to compensate for slip/skid compensation during turning (similar "
"to differential aileron)."
msgstr ""
"普通飞翼飞机使用两个控制面作为升降副翼来控制俯仰和横滚。在某些情况下，会在翼尖小翼上增加方向舵来控制偏航。差动扰流板通过将升降副翼分成 4 "
"个独立控制面来发挥优势：正常的升降副翼功能保留用于俯仰和横滚控制，而偏航控制则通过使用机翼一侧的两个控制面产生阻力来实现，从而模拟方向舵控制。若校准正确，可确保飞行员在起飞和降落时通过方向舵输入获得流畅的偏航控制，同时允许飞行员在转弯时补偿侧滑（类似于差动副翼）。"

